Here is the commit message:
Fix signedness error introduced by 599b800b, also fix
 spacing.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a signedness error introduced in a previous commit, which likely resulted from passing an argument of an incorrect type to the `NET_SetOOBHeader` function. This could lead to unexpected behavior or crashes due to type mismatches in pointer handling.

Here is the patch:
 	char    string[ MAX_MSGLEN ];

-	NET_SetOOBHeader(string);
+	NET_SetOOBHeader( string );

 	va_start( argptr, format );
 /*
 ===============
-NET_OutOfBandPrint
+NET_OutOfBandData

 Sends a data message in an out-of-band datagram (only used for "connect")
 */
 void QDECL NET_OutOfBandData( netsrc_t sock, netadr_t adr, byte *format, int len )
 {
 	byte  string[ MAX_MSGLEN * 2 ];
 	int   i;
 	msg_t mbuf;

-	NET_SetOOBHeader(string);
+	NET_SetOOBHeader( ( char * ) string );

 	for ( i = 0; i < len; i++ )
 	{
 		string[ i + 4 ] = format[ i ];
 	}

 	mbuf.data = string;
 	mbuf.cursize = len + 4;
 	Huff_Compress( &mbuf, 12 );
 	// send the datagram
 	NET_SendPacket( sock, mbuf.cursize, mbuf.data, adr );
 }



